    {
      "id": "doc_1",
      "title": "🚀 Ajaia Product Spec: AI-Assisted Document Platform",
      "content": "<h1>Ajaia Product Spec: AI-Assisted Document Platform</h1><p><strong>Status:</strong> In Review &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Author:</strong> Alice Walker &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Target Release:</strong> Q4 2026</p><hr><h2>1. Executive Summary</h2><p>Modern product teams lose dozens of hours every sprint bouncing between disconnected tools for drafting specs, design reviews, and engineering RFCs. <em>Ajaia Docs</em> unifies rich collaborative drafting, structured file attachments, and instant teammate sharing into a single, cohesive canvas.aodifidhfoonkkjkjkjkjkjhjkhkjknn</p><blockquote><p>\"Our goal is to make document creation as fast as thinking, with zero friction in teammate handoffs</p></blockquote><h2>2. Core Functional Requirements</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Rich Formatting Engine:</strong> Headings, clean typography, bold/italic accents, formatted lists, and code blocks.</p></li><li><p><strong>Native File Imports:</strong> Direct ingestion of Markdown and plaintext files straight into editable live docs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lightweight Access Control:</strong> Distinct Owner, Editor, and Viewer permissions with real-time UI state reflect.</p></li><li><p><strong>Resilient Local Persistence:</strong> Automated debounced saving ensuring zero state loss across reloads.</p></li></ul><h2>3. Key Success Metrics</h2><ol><li><p>Document creation time decreased by <strong>45%</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Cross-functional review turnaround within <strong>24 hours</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Zero accidental document overwrite incidents via explicit access roles.</p></li></ol><pre><code>// Example Share Payload Contract\nPOST /api/documents/doc_1/share\n{\n  \"targetEmail\": \"bob@ajaia.io\",\n  \"accessLevel\": \"editor\"\n}</code></pre><p>Please review and leave feedback or suggest edits directly!</p>",
      "ownerId": "user_alice",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-18T10:00:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-20T06:50:27.647Z",
      "wordCount": 184,
      "characterCount": 1403,
